"""Single-rule mutants for the signed-candidate receiver: the candidate
journal and its store bookkeeping, the replay index, evaluation, supersession,
the operator verbs, the candidate view's gate, the inbound poll, the host
intakes and their tombstones, the receiver's clock, and the delegation
config's inbound members (`router/peerjournal.py`, `peerclock.py`,
`peerbind.py`, `peerlane.py`, `config.py`), each run against the tests that
name it.

Run from the repository root:

    python3 -B router/tests/mutate_peerjournal.py

Same discipline as `mutate_pathcanon.py`: bytecode caching OFF and
`__pycache__` cleared before each run, every file restored after; every
named test must pass unmutated first, and a mutant is RED only when unittest
reports a FAILURE of the named test (an ERROR is printed and is not red).
A mutant may edit more than one place when a rule has two guards. Exit 0
only when every mutant turns every named test red. Not a test module itself.

Recorded as EQUIVALENT, so not run:
- dropping `candidate_view`'s own minor test in `peerlane.candidate_view_of`:
  both names share the (3, 4) minor, so the vocabulary's gate turns the view
  OFF first;
- dropping only ONE of a host intake's two pruning guards (every listed name
  counts; any unreadable entry makes the listing incomplete): either guard
  alone keeps the tombstone, so each is run with the other dropped too;
- dropping only `rebuild_meta`'s keep-the-old-frontier branch: the fallback
  recomputes the same contiguous settled prefix from disk in every reachable
  state, so the frontier's reset is run with both branches broken.
"""
